# Netlify/Cloudflare Pages production routes.
#
# The `!` suffix forces the rule to win over a file that physically exists at
# the same path. Netlify skips an unforced rule whenever the path matches a
# real file, which would leave the root `index.html` fallback page served at
# `/` instead of redirecting to `/business`.
/business   /business/index.html   200!
/ca-firms   /ca-firms/index.html   200!
/pricing    /pricing/index.html    200!
/pricing.html   /pricing           301!
/index.html     /business          308!
/               /business          308!
